.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 8.2% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+12.2% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 11%.","Capex runs only 0.0x depreciation (0.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own 12.9%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 57%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (14 sales, net $9.7M sold).","It returns 18.1% a year to shareholders (18.1% in buybacks).","The share count has grown 5.3% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 697 employees, each generates about $1.1M of revenue, 3.0x the Healthcare median, and productivity has risen 7.7% a year.","That works out to $236K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.4M (3x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $110K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":55,"head":"Avoid: Altman Z in the distress zone (0.62).","pros":["Trades 44% below fair value of $6.27","FCF margin 20.6%","Revenue grew 7.7%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 1.3x","P/FCF 7.3x vs sector 23.7x"],"cons":["ROIC 2.8% vs WACC 9.2%","Interest coverage only 2.1x","Altman Z in the distress zone (0.62)","P/E 70.2x vs sector 25.5x","Heavy insider selling ($9.7M net over 12 months)"],"flags":["Altman Z in the distress zone (0.62)"],"need":[],"buy_below":5.33,"vc":{"base":6.27,"base_src":"dcf","bear":4.86,"bull":8.32,"alt_median":1.13,"n_alt":1,"gap":4.5517,"dispersion":0.6947,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (69% dispersion)","DCF is 455% above the other models' median ($1.13)"]},"med":{"pe":25.5,"ev_ebitda":15.7195,"pfcf":23.7283,"pb":3.5607,"roic":-0.1181,"gross_margin":0.5566,"fcf_margin":0.0285,"div_yield":0.014}},"ticker":"GDRX","date":"2026-11-06"}